# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Byte preservation.
#
# This is a reproducibility package: preprint/results/checksums.sha256 is only
# useful to a reader if every file checks out with exactly the bytes that were
# hashed. Git's end-of-line translation would break that under Windows, or
# anywhere core.autocrlf is enabled, and Level 1 verifies frozen inputs by
# SHA-256, so the failure would look like a scientific problem when it is not.
#
# Everything is therefore checked out verbatim.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* -text

# Binary containers, marked explicitly for clarity and for diff behaviour.
*.png binary
*.pdf binary

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Redistribution boundary (see DATA_LICENSES.md section 3).
#
# The reconstructed Therapeutics Data Commons reference tables are not
# redistributed. They are absent from this repository and gitignored; these
# rules are declared defensively so that no archive produced by `git archive`
# -- the mechanism behind GitHub release assets and Zenodo archiving -- could
# carry them if one were ever introduced locally.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
validation/external_prediction/training_reference/ export-ignore
validation/external_prediction/training_reference/*.csv export-ignore
